## Summary of changes

Three files modified — the fix eliminates the TOCTOU race by reversing the order of operations:

### Root cause
The original flow: **check stock → charge → decrement**. Between `check_stock` and `decrement`, all concurrent orders see stock as available, get charged, then race to decrement. Losers are charged but deliver nothing.

### Fix

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `inventory.py:18-29` | Added `reserve(quantity)` and `cancel_reservation(quantity)` — wrap check+decrement in an `asyncio.Lock` so only one order can decrement at a time |
| `checkout.py:11-27` | New flow: **reserve → charge → release on failure**. Stock is secured *before* payment, so every charge is backed by confirmed inventory |
| `payments.py:18-24` | Added `_processed: Set[str]` — `charge()` returns `True` if the same `order_id` was already charged (defense-in-depth idempotency) |

### Invariant verification (10/10 runs, all pass)
- `stock >= 0` always — reserve prevents overselling
- `total_charged == successful * price` — no ghost charges
- `duplicates == 0` — no double-charges
